## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a robust, real-time BSS pipeline under practical failures: partial sensor dropout, dynamic source counts, and mobile platforms.

## Key Concepts
- Adaptive time-frequency representation and frame sizing for non-stationary noise
- Sensor-reliability weighted whitening to tolerate dropout
- Demixing with per-bin ICA vs joint diagonalization under varying source counts
- Cross-bin permutation tracking to prevent misalignment across frequencies
- Online model-order selection and latency considerations for edge devices

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code skeleton for online ICA frame processing
function processFrame(frame, state){
  const wf = adaptiveSTFT(frame, state.window);
  const whitened = whiten(wf, state.weights);
  const sources = perBinICA(whitened, state.demixer);
  const permuted = crossBinPermute(sources, state.tracker);
  return updateState(state, permuted);
}
```

